Hi Janice,

Thank you for meeting this morning. I have attached our record of the 11:00 a=
greement, ELM-BSC-2026-AGR-001 v1.0.

We have 36 planned places for Reading Conditions at Work. Participants will w=
rite a decision memo connecting the applicable provision and the reception re=
cord to their advice. The separate return will show enrolment at the deadline=
, valid submitters and those meeting the standard; any attainment rate will u=
se enrolment as its denominator.

For Building Proposals from Evidence we have 24 planned places. Participants =
will submit a recommendation to the desk lead, with evidence, an alternative =
and a response to an unconfirmed assumption. Its return will show enrolment a=
nd valid submitters, then the number of valid submitters whose writing includ=
es all three aspects. We will keep the reporting fields separate and will not=
 combine the rates. These places are capacity, not participation or results.

Brookdale will coordinate nominations and Elmwood will prepare and deliver th=
e courses and compile the returns. The next step is to introduce the colleagu=
es responsible for nominations and course administration so they can agree ho=
w the nominations will reach us.

Best,
Heather


On Tue, 7 Apr 2026 at 09:12, Janice Mitchell <janice@brookdale-service.exampl=
e> wrote:
> Hi Heather,
>
> Before we meet at 11:00, could you help me describe what we would receive i=
f we contract for 36 places on Reading Conditions at Work and 24 on Building =
Proposals from Evidence?
>
> I need to explain the two pieces separately here. For the reception staff, =
I want to be able to show that they can identify the provision that applies t=
o a decision. For the team leads, I want to show that they can compare altern=
atives and make a recommendation. What would participants produce in each cou=
rse, and what could you report back to us?
>
> Thank you,
> Janice
>
> Janice Mitchell
> Brookdale Service Cooperative

